    #  YA. The phase, the log directory, the subjects, the script directory
    #      (<scripts>, <home>/.cache/emend-build/m3p6-p4/scripts, on the disk)
    #      and the keep (m3p6-p4/keep-host) are this phase's; the base is P3's
    #      record commit ("M3 part 6 P3 record:"); the phase commit is P4's
    #      catalogue and probes commit by its subject ("M3 part 6 P4: the
    #      catalogue and limits, the probes"); the four samples each have a run
    #      directory <runs>/<date>-<sha>-<sample> and a record stem
    #      m3p6-p4-<sample>-<date>-<sha> (the spec's names, "P4"); SAMPLES is
    #      still the copy sample, whose checks are P3's, and RERUNS the three
    #      earlier samples; SUPERSEDED_RUN names the four by their common stem;
    #      the spec pinned through SPEC_SHA at P4's doc commit, planning's
    #      rulings during P4 standing uncommitted in the working tree's copy,
    #      printed. The usage takes the size.log as its third argument.
    #  YB. Change XB's form: the committed open-check record the keep is
    #      compared with is P3's, the last committed, named by its record
    #      commit, resolved by its subject ("M3 part 6 P3 record:"; no hash is
    #      typed here); it is the base itself, the parent of P4's doc commit; the
    #      control names the doc commit instead. P3_REC names the same commit,
    #      the one whose run directories the four samples are compared with
